WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.538
Open WebUI can support document and knowledge workflows where uploaded material is

00:00:04.538 --> 00:00:06.757
used as context for model responses.

00:00:06.757 --> 00:00:08.237
At a high level,

00:00:08.237 --> 00:00:13.785
retrieval-augmented generation involves indexing or retrieving relevant content and placing it into the model's context.

00:00:13.785 --> 00:00:16.374
Embeddings help represent text for similarity search.

00:00:16.374 --> 00:00:18.963
This can make private documents more usable,

00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:21.922
but it also creates new data handling responsibilities.

00:00:21.922 --> 00:00:24.511
Document sensitivity should be considered before upload.

00:00:24.511 --> 00:00:28.209
Files may contain personal information, client data, business plans, credentials,

00:00:28.209 --> 00:00:30.798
internal procedures, regulated content, or proprietary research.

00:00:30.798 --> 00:00:35.976
Once uploaded, they may be stored, indexed, backed up, searched, or reused in conversations.

00:00:35.976 --> 00:00:39.675
Treat document features as part of a data management system,

00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:41.524
not just a convenience button.

00:00:41.524 --> 00:00:44.113
Source organization improves retrieval quality and review.

00:00:44.113 --> 00:00:48.182
Knowledge collections should have clear names, purpose, ownership, and freshness expectations.

00:00:48.182 --> 00:00:50.401
Stale documents can produce outdated answers.

00:00:50.401 --> 00:00:53.360
Inaccurate retrieval can surface irrelevant or conflicting material.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.798
Retrieved content should be treated as evidence for the model to use,

00:00:57.798 --> 00:00:58.908
not unquestioned truth.

00:00:58.908 --> 00:01:00.387
Retention and cleanup matter.

00:01:00.387 --> 00:01:04.456
Decide how long uploaded documents should remain, who can access them,

00:01:04.456 --> 00:01:08.524
how they are removed, and whether backups preserve them after deletion.

00:01:08.524 --> 00:01:09.634
For important workflows,

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:14.072
users should be able to trace an answer back to source material

00:01:14.072 --> 00:01:16.661
and understand whether the source is current.

00:01:16.661 --> 00:01:19.620
Retrieval is most valuable when it remains auditable.
